/* Deep lessons — Sorting algoritmlari (sorting).
 *
 * Eight algorithms and the ideas around them, taught in the order that makes
 * each one answer a complaint about the one before it: selection wastes
 * comparisons, bubble wastes swaps, insertion is fast only when the input is
 * nearly sorted, merge fixes the worst case but pays memory, quick gives the
 * memory back but risks n², heap gives up the risk, and counting escapes the
 * comparison bound entirely.
 *
 * Every stage gets a picture of its own kind: bars where heights carry the
 * meaning, a tree for the heap, labelled regions for an invariant, two streams
 * for a merge, containers for counting. Fifteen identical rows of boxes would
 * teach nothing after the second one.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

